WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.450
A new trailer’s out for Westworld Season
2 and it hints at some of the themes that

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.390
we’ll see in series ahead.

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:10.559
If you haven’t seen our Season 1 video,
you might wanna watch that first.

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:15.429
In this trailer, Dolores talks about burning
down the human world and building a “new

00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:20.650
world” where the hosts – the robots – can
be free . So Dolores seems to be waging war

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:25.420
against the humans remaining in Westworld
– we see her gunning down fleeing people,

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.400
like something outta Planet of the Apes.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:33.010
Her victims run away – which makes the Kanye
soundtrack all the more appropriate.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.250
Dolores isn’t alone in her war.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.571
She’s got her sidekick Teddy, who mostly
just follows her round and looks upset, but

00:00:39.571 --> 00:00:42.550
she also has these mysterious masked men.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:46.480
We’re actually told who these guys are back
in Season 1.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.730
Charlotte mentions that as part of his final
narrative, Ford created “a horde of masked

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:56.940
men” who support Wyatt . And Wyatt, remember,
is like the big bad guy role from years ago

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.510
that’s now been embraced by Dolores.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:05.290
So presumably, these masked men help Dolores
in her fight for freedom against the humans.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:10.280
But that raises the question – if this whole
story of Wyatt and the masked men was planned

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:16.340
out by Ford – is Dolores really free, or
is she still under Ford’s control, even

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.689
after his death?

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:20.840
Maeve also attacks humans.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.590
She uses robot bulls to kill security guys
in the Mesa Hub, and there’s also a fight

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:29.319
in the Control Room where Maeve meets Sizemore
last trailer.

00:01:29.319 --> 00:01:33.850
The bull thing calls back to something Dolores
said last season – when you herd cattle,

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.690
there’s a “Judas steer” that all the
others cows follow.

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:42.619
Maybe Maeve is the Judas steer leading the
other hosts to consciousness and freedom.

00:01:42.619 --> 00:01:47.659
But thing is, while the cattle follow the
Judas steer, the Judas steer is controlled

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:53.240
by the human cattle rancher – just as Ford
seems to be controlling Maeve and Dolores.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:57.590
So again, Ford’s ghost looms over the story
still.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:02.299
Another explanation for the bulls is that
last season, Maeve is upgraded with the ability

00:02:02.299 --> 00:02:08.080
to control other hosts – she uses this on
a sheriff, and even on Bernard.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.610
This power might be how Maeve controls these
bulls, which is super cool – for her to

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:17.940
control an animal army, like she was Ant Man
or Squirrel Girl or some homicidal version

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.130
of Snow White.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:24.100
But if Maeve represents freedom, isn’t it
wrong for her to control other hosts like

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.490
this, to take away their freedom?

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:30.780
Again it’s kinda like how Ford gives hosts
freedom by manipulating them.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:31.780
Anyway.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:37.100
Maeve’s goal, at the end of Season 1, is
to find her host daughter somewhere in a park.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.180
What will happen when Maeve finds her?

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.490
What kind of relationship can you have with
a daughter who’s a robot, whose memories

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:45.810
and behaviours are programmed?

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.470
How do you love a machine?

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:53.450
There are lots of cool questions to explore
around relationships among robots and humans.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:58.340
While Maeve and Dolores cause chaos and violence,
some surviving human staff are with Bernard.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:04.090
It’ll be cool to see how these humans react
if they find out their boss Bernard is a host.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:09.160
The staff see bodies on the shore of Westworld
– which might be what’s left after Dolores’

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.880
massacre last season.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.570
We also see Bernard with a big faceless host
who attacks someone.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:19.670
Is this like an experimental robot, maybe
a military thing?

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:24.320
We keep hearing last season that the Delos
company has some special secret business interest

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:29.650
that goes deeper than tourism . Maybe this
creepy robot is related.

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:35.510
We also see the host Peter Abernathy captured
in the Mesa Hub, which is weird – cause

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:40.240
last we saw Peter, he was sent out of Westworld
by Charlotte and Sizemore, who were using

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:45.670
Peter’s brain to smuggle data . If Pete
left the park, why’s he back here?

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:48.060
Maybe this shot happens in the past.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:53.190
Because there’s also this shot of Logan,
young Logan, as he looked thirty years ago

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.470
with William.

00:03:54.470 --> 00:04:00.030
It looks like Season 2 continues to tell this
story in multiple timeframes at once – there’s

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:05.252
the present, with Maeve and Dolores’ uprising,
and the past with William and Logan in early

00:04:05.252 --> 00:04:06.790
Westworld thirty years ago.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:11.270
Maybe we’ll find out more about how Delos
bought Westworld, and how William took control

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.670
over Logan.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:17.150
This particular shot looks like Logan’s
in the real world, outside of Westworld, cause

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.500
there’re city skyscapes behind him.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:23.409
This might be New York, like in the photo
of Logan’s sister Juliet.

00:04:23.409 --> 00:04:29.210
But the people around Logan in this shot appear
to be hosts, cause they’re all frozen – so

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:33.990
this is not only the first time we’ve seen
the real world outside Westworld, but we’re

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:36.030
seeing hosts in the real world.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:40.139
What kind of role do robots play in this future
society?

00:04:40.139 --> 00:04:43.830
What kinda technology, and culture might we
see?

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:49.020
This shot also might be in the past – it
looks like Arnold with an early Dolores, so

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.580
maybe we’ll see more of their backstory.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:56.680
Dolores wears a dress and hair similar to
Angela in Season 1 Episode 2.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:00.939
Maybe Dolores was originally gonna be a greeter
host like Angela.

00:05:00.939 --> 00:05:06.680
Also remember that Peter is Dolores’ host
father, so maybe we’ll see more of their

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:07.680
relationship.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:12.770
We’ll also see more of young William, and
his present self, the Man in Black.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:17.740
Last season, William wanted real danger and
violence in Westworld, and now with Dolores’

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:20.250
war he’s got his wish.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:25.300
His role last season was to show how dark
and empty humans can be.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.610
Maybe next season will be an opportunity for
William to change – to believe in something

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:33.009
more than just fighting and winning.

00:05:33.009 --> 00:05:37.949
We see hosts from Ghost Nation, a mysterious
tribe of native Americans in the Westworld

00:05:37.949 --> 00:05:38.949
park.

00:05:38.949 --> 00:05:42.590
They captured Stubbs last season, and might
have him still.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:47.659
But their role in the story could go deeper
– we saw last season that these guys know

00:05:47.659 --> 00:05:53.550
things about the maze , and about shades . They
also scalp people, which is interesting cause

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:57.229
it was in a scalp that we first saw the symbol
of the Maze.

00:05:57.229 --> 00:06:01.699
So it’s not clear what side Ghost Nation
will take in Dolores and Maeve’s conflicts,

00:06:01.699 --> 00:06:05.340
but it’ll be cool to learn more about what
they know.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.840
We also see this dog or “wolf” walking
around.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:13.389
It looks like the same one that appears in
the Season 1 finale and in Season 1 Episode

00:06:13.389 --> 00:06:14.389
2.

00:06:14.389 --> 00:06:17.300
Why does this wolf keep turning up at massacres?

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:20.139
Is it wandering across from the Game of Thrones
set?

00:06:20.139 --> 00:06:24.669
You can actually see a wolf’s head in this
shot of Arnold and early Dolores – so maybe

00:06:24.669 --> 00:06:28.979
this wolf is a host that’s been wandering
round for the last thirty years?

00:06:28.979 --> 00:06:31.020
It’s very odd.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:36.090
So there are lots of little miscellaneous
mysteries in this show, and we might not get

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:38.270
good answers to all of them.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:41.379
But there is grand broader story.

00:06:41.379 --> 00:06:46.720
The central image of this trailer is the clash
of these robot bulls against human soldiers,

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:49.990
which perfectly captures the conflict explored
in this series.

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:55.069
It’s about freedom versus control, and the
real versus the artificial – and it’s

00:06:55.069 --> 00:06:58.069
increasingly hard to tell which is which.

00:06:58.069 --> 00:07:03.780
The robots are machines but they seem wild
and free, like Dolores and Maeve.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:08.999
These soldiers are the real humans but they
seem cold, faceless and dehumanised – like

00:07:08.999 --> 00:07:10.590
the Man in Black.

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:15.800
Westworld Season 1 is described as a “prequel”
or a “prologue” to the greater story – it

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:18.199
introduces the characters, world and themes.

00:07:18.199 --> 00:07:21.240
But Season 2 is where the clash happens.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:26.689
Man and machine, Westworld and East world,
present and past – all come together at

00:07:26.689 --> 00:07:27.860
last.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:31.699
Season 2 begins on April 22.

